    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly are delighted to present No. 35 Sandymount to the market, a most impressive Victorian family residence, enjoying magnificent sea views and retaining a wealth of fine period features synonymous with the architecture of the era. Presented in pristine decorative order throughout, this handsome residence combines elegant, generously proportioned accommodation with a wonderful south westerly rear garden and an enviable coastal setting.\r\n\r\nThe property is approached via a landscaped front garden, with a paved pathway and granite steps leading to an attractive entrance vestibule. This in turn opens through to the impressive hall door, complete with a beautiful stained-glass fanlight. The elegant entrance hall features a marble floor, high ceilings, ornate cornicing and centre rose, setting the tone for the accommodation beyond. Two beautifully proportioned reception rooms are positioned off the hall, both featuring original period fireplaces and polished timber flooring, with the drawing room enjoying superb sea views.\r\n\r\nMoving to the first floor return, there is a separate shower room and a well-appointed study/home office with its own balcony, enjoying south westerly views towards the Dublin Mountains. On the first floor, there are two generous double bedrooms, with the magnificent principal bedroom spanning the full width of the house and enjoying wonderful views towards Poolbeg Lighthouse and as far as Howth Head. This fine room also benefits from a large walk-in wardrobe and ensuite, while the second bedroom overlooks the rear garden.\r\n\r\nReturning to the hall floor return, Bedroom 3 provides a further generous double bedroom, with an adjacent shower room.\r\n\r\nThe garden level provides excellent additional living accommodation and benefits from its own separate entrance. The accommodation comprises an entrance hall with under-stairs storage, utility/boot room with marble tiled floor, family room with attractive marble fireplace and sea views, and a superbly appointed kitchen with an excellent range of hand-painted wall and floor units.  Double doors lead through to the conservatory/sunroom, with sliding patio doors providing direct access to the rear garden. Bedroom 4 and a downstairs WC completes the accommodation at this level.\r\n\r\nThe south westerly rear garden is a particular feature of this fine home, enjoying an excellent degree of sunshine and providing a wonderful private setting for outdoor entertaining and relaxation. A ceramic-tiled patio and BBQ area take full advantage of the sunny aspect, while vehicular rear access provides parking for one car and leads to a substantial block-built garden store. To the front, the landscaped garden is mainly laid in lawn with a low-maintenance rockery and flower beds, with granite steps providing an attractive approach to the hall door and a separate access to the garden level.\r\n\r\nAll in all, No. 35 Sandymount is a most impressive period residence of distinction, full of warmth and character whilst combining elegant Victorian proportions, fine original features, excellent family accommodation and magnificent sea views in one of Dublin’s most sought-after coastal locations.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended.\r\n\r\nMore about the location....\r\n\r\nSituated directly on Sandymount Strand, the property enjoys immediate access to scenic coastal walks and is within strolling distance of Sandymount Village with its cafés, restaurants, and boutiques. Sydney Parade DART station and multiple bus routes provide seamless connectivity. Nearby amenities include Westwood Leisure Centre, Claremont Tennis Club, Railway Union grounds, the RDS, and the Aviva Stadium, while the city centre, IFSC, and Dublin Airport are all easily accessible. Some of the capitals best schools are close by including St. Michael's, Blackrock and St. Andrews colleges."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Vestibule\r\n(17.5m x 1.05m)\r\nApproached via granite steps with a traditional handrail. marble floor and hall door with an original stained glass fan light.\r\n\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall\r\n(10m x 1.75m)\r\nWelcoming entrance hall with original ornate cornice and centre rose detailing. Marble floor.\r\n\r\nDrawing Room\r\n(4.85m x 4.85m)\r\nElegantly proportioned overlooking Dublin Bay, featuring an original marble open fireplace with a cast iron and tiled inset. Decorative cornice, centre rose, window shutters and polished floorboards. Double doors to..\r\n\r\n\r\nDining Room\r\n(4.75m x 4.75m)\r\nFeature original fireplace with a cast iron inset, decorative cornice, centre rose, and window shutters. Polished floorboards.\r\n\r\nHall Floor Return\r\n\r\n\r\nInner Hall\r\n(1.25m x 1.3m)\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\n(3.05m x 3.6m)\r\nDouble bedroom overlooking the rear garden. Built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\n\r\nShower Room\r\n(1.65m x 1.7m)\r\nWHB set in a vanity unit, WD and step in shower enclosure with a power shower. Recessed spot lights, tiled floor and walls.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Return\r\n\r\n\r\nShower Room\r\n(1.85m x 1.35m)\r\nExtensively tiled with a WHB set in a vanity unit, WC and step in shower enclosure with a power shower. Recessed spot lights.\r\n\r\n\r\nStudy / Home Office\r\n(3.40m x 2.25m)\r\nLight filled study with a built in bookcase, solid oak flooring and recessed spot lights. Sliding patio door to..\r\n\r\nBalcony\r\n(3.3m x 1.3m)\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\n(6.8m x 4.8m)\r\nStunning principal bedroom suite, spanning the width of the house with two large windows overlooking Dublin Bay. Decorative coving, centre rose and window shutters. Two sets of built in alcove wardrobes.\r\n\r\nEnsuite\r\n(2.1m x 1.25m)\r\nExtensively tiled with a WHB set in a vanity unit, WC, step in shower enclosure with a power shower, heated towel rail and Velux window.\r\n\r\nWalk in Wardrobe\r\n(2.35m x 1.35m)\r\nExtensive range of built in hanging and shelving. Recessed spot lights and Velux window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\n(4.6m x 3.3m)\r\nLarge double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, with ceiling coving, and window shutters.\r\n\r\nGarden Level\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall\r\n(1.5m x 1.3m)\r\nGarden level entrance with under steps storage which houses the gas fired central heating boiler.\r\n\r\nUtility/ Boot Room\r\n(3.15m x 1.6m)\r\nPlumbing for washing machine/dryer, with marble tiled floor, fitted wall and floor press units and hot press with dual immersion. Door into:\r\n\r\n\r\nInner Hall\r\n(6.2m x 1.2m)\r\nWith marble tiled floor.\r\n\r\n\r\nFamily Room\r\n(4.65m x 4.5m)\r\nFeature marble fireplace with a gas fire inset, window shutters, recessed spot lights, built in study desk with overhead shelving and hatch to\r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen / Breakfast Room\r\n(4.65m x 4.5m)\r\nExcellent range of built in wall and floor units complemented by a marble counter top and a mosaic tiled splash back. Appliances to include a 5 ring Ide range cooker with extractor fan, dishwasher, Fisher & Paykel fridge/freezer, recessed spot lights, marble tiled floor and double-glazed doors leading through to a:\r\n\r\n\r\nSun Room / TV Room\r\n(5.05m x 3.4)\r\nWith marble tiled floor and sliding patio door leading out to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nDownstairs WC\r\n\r\nWith WHB WC and tiled floor.\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 4\r\n5.36m x 3.1m)\r\nLarge double bedroom overlooking the rear garden, built in wardrobes and study desk.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nTo the front there is a low maintenance walled front garden set mainly in lawn with surround flower beds and rockery with paved pedestrian access leading up to a set of granite steps which in turn lead up to the hall door and a set of steps leading down to the garden level entrance with bin store off.\r\n\r\nThe walled rear garden measures approximately 22.35m (73’4”) in length x 6.70m (22') in width, is a particular selling feature of the property with a sunny south westerly facing aspect, vehicular rear access with off-street car parking. The rear garden is beautifully landscaped mainly in lawn with an abundance of mature flower beds, trees, granite walls, ceramic patio, and BBQ area ideal for relaxing in the lovely evenings all year round particularly in the Spring and Summer. There is also outdoor lighting and a water tap.\r\n\r\nGarden Store: 2.60m x 3.25m (8'6\" x 10'8\") block built with electricity."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Magnificent mid-terrace Victorian residence.\r\nExceptional sea views towards Poolbeg Lighthouse and Howth Head.\r\nBeautifully retained period features throughout.\r\nTwo elegant reception rooms with original marble fireplaces.\r\nPrincipal bedroom spanning the full width of the house with walk-in wardrobe and ensuite.\r\nSeparate study/home office with private balcony and views towards the Dublin Mountains.\r\nPrivate south westerly rear garden with patio, BBQ area and vehicular rear access.\r\nHighly sought-after Sandymount location, moments from the village, strand and DART station.\r\nOff street car parking for one car to the rear.\r\nGas Fired Central Heating.\r\nDouble glazed pvc windows throughout.\r\nResidential on street disc parking."
